        }
      ],
      "description": "Test-only bootstrap, not a player action: hiring already grants the Rookie starting qualification (ROLE_STARTING_QUALIFICATION in Employee.ts, same for the UI hire button and this console command), so this only raises the level for the scenario's needs. No role tag -- there is no UI control for this and none should exist; the player-facing way to raise a skill is `employee train` at a training building. Command mode keeps running it unchanged; interaction mode keeps it as an unmarked (legacy) command step. Finding #15 class: the original command used positional args (`employee assign_skill 1 geology 5`) — assignSkillCommand requires the named form and silently rejected it ('Usage: employee assign_skill <id> skill:<category> level:1-5', never thrown), so this call and the one below failed on every run in this file's history. Fixed to the correct syntax.",
      "expect": {
        "equals": {
          "proficiencyTotal": 6
        },
        "note": "employee 1 (Rookie 1) -> level 5, employee 2 stays Rookie 1: 5+1=6"
      }
